---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { EMAIL } from '../../consts';
---

<Base title="Mellow privacy policy" description="Privacy policy for Mellow for Google Docs, the dark mode and writer sidebar extension.">
  <h1>Mellow privacy policy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 28 October 2026</p>

    <p>
      Mellow is a Chrome extension for Google Docs™. It adds a dark theme and a writer sidebar
      (chapters, notes and a daily word goal).
    </p>

    <h2>What Mellow collects</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. Mellow does not collect, sell or share any personal data, document content, browsing
      history or usage analytics, and it has no servers of its own.
    </p>

    <h2>What Mellow stores</h2>
    <p>Everything below is saved in your own Chrome profile using Chrome's built-in storage:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your settings: dark mode and the writer sidebar on or off, and which sidebar tab is open.</li>
      <li>Your note cards and word goal for each document, kept on this computer only.</li>
      <li>If you use Mellow Pro: your licence key and whether it is active.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Uninstalling Mellow removes all of it.</p>

    <h2>Where Mellow runs</h2>
    <p>
      Only on Google Docs document pages (docs.google.com/document). It changes colours on your
      screen, and it reads the headings and word count that Docs already displays so it can show
      them in the sidebar. It does not change your documents or send their contents anywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>Licence checks</h2>
    <p>
      Mellow makes a network request only if you activate Mellow Pro. It then sends your licence
      key and an anonymous device label to Polar, which sells Mellow Pro, to confirm the key is
      valid, and re-checks it about once a day. Nothing from your documents is included. Polar
      handles this under its own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      Mellow Pro and the optional supporter link use a checkout run by Polar, which handles payment
      under its own privacy policy. Mellow itself never sees payment details.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a></p>

    <p><a href="/mellow/">About Mellow</a></p>

    <p class="muted">Google Docs is a trademark of Google LLC. Mellow is not affiliated with Google.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
